FeedImportFieldRef = Product ref (new products)
FeedImportFieldWeight = Weight (kg)
FeedImportFieldSellPrice = Selling price
FeedImportFieldBuyPrice = Buy price (supplier price)
FeedImportFieldMinQty = Minimum purchase quantity
FeedImportFieldStock = Stock available at the supplier
FeedImportExtrafield = Extra field
FeedImportWarningNoSku = No field is mapped to the SKU: the feed cannot be imported. Use "Fetch & preview" to read the feed's fields, or upload a schema.
FeedImportWarningNoLabel = No field is mapped to the label: new items will go to the review queue instead of being created.
FeedImportHost = Server
FeedImportPasswordUnchanged = (unchanged)
FeedImportClearPassword = Remove the password
FeedImportDirectory = Directory
FeedImportDirectoryHelp = Directory of the file on the server. Starting with /: from the root of the server; otherwise from the login's home directory.
FeedImportPattern = File name
FeedImportPatternHelp = The file's name, or a pattern: * and ? as wildcards (the newest matching file is taken), and {YYYY} {YY} {MM} {DD} {YYYYMMDD} for today's date, e.g. stock_{YYYYMMDD}.csv. Email: the name the attachment must match; empty = any .csv or .xml file, according to the file type.
FeedImportPassive = Passive mode
FeedImportInsecure = Accept any certificate
FeedImportInsecureHelp = Do not check the server's TLS certificate (self-signed or expired certificates). The connection is still encrypted, but not protected against interception.
FeedImportHostKey = Server key fingerprint
FeedImportHostKeyHelp = Fingerprint of the server's SSH key, in MD5 (79:ea:b1:...). When it is set, the connection is refused if the server's key differs, which protects the password from a server impersonating the supplier's. Test connection shows the server's fingerprint: check it with the supplier, then copy it here. A SHA256 fingerprint can only be checked if PHP's curl is built with libssh2.
FeedImportHostKeyMissing = The server's identity is not checked. Use Test connection to get its fingerprint, check it with the supplier, and enter it here.
FeedImportHostKeyLearnt = The server's key fingerprint is %s. Check it with the supplier, then enter it in "Server key fingerprint" so the server is checked at every connection.
FeedImportErrorHostKeyMd5 = This server's curl (built with libssh) can only check MD5 fingerprints of SFTP servers. Enter the MD5 fingerprint (Test connection shows it, or: ssh-keyscan host | ssh-keygen -l -E md5 -f -).
FeedImportUrlHelp = Full URL of the file, with any key the supplier gives in it. Date tokens ({YYYYMMDD}...) are replaced. Login and password, if set, are sent as HTTP basic authentication.
FeedImportEmailSetup = Email Collector
FeedImportEmailSaveFirst = Save the feed first: its number is needed to set up the Email Collector.
FeedImportEmailHelp = In Home > Setup > Email Collectors, create a collector for the mailbox the supplier sends to (or use an existing one), with filters on the sender or subject as needed. Add the operation <strong>%s</strong> with the parameter %s (this feed's number). The attachment matching the file name above is kept, and imported by the next run of the scheduled job (within 15 minutes) or by Run now.
FeedImportEmailOperation = Feed import: import the attached file
FeedImportEmailCollectors = Email Collectors
FeedImportEmailWaiting = File received by email, waiting to be imported: %s (%s).
FeedImportEmailErrorFeed = Feed import: "%s" is not the number of a feed. Give the feed's number as the operation's parameter.
FeedImportEmailErrorNotEmail = Feed import: the feed "%s" is not set to receive its file by email.
FeedImportEmailErrorDisabled = Feed import: the feed "%s" is disabled.
FeedImportEmailErrorNoAttachment = Feed import: no attachment of this email matches "%s" for the feed "%s". Attachments: %s
FeedImportUploadHelp = The file is imported with "Import a file" below.
FeedImportSchedule = Schedule
FeedImportScheduleManual = By hand only
FeedImportScheduleDaily = Every day
FeedImportScheduleHours = Every N hours
FeedImportScheduleTime = at
FeedImportScheduleDailyAt = Every day at %s
FeedImportScheduleEveryHours = Every %s hours
FeedImportScheduleEmail = When the file arrives by email
FeedImportScheduleEmailHelp = When the file arrives: the Email Collector's own scheduled job decides how often the mailbox is read, then this module's job imports the file (every 15 minutes).
FeedImportPacing = Pacing
FeedImportPacingHelp = Spreads a large import over time instead of loading the server all at once: after every block of rows that change something (created, updated, stock corrected, sent to review, set to 0), the import pauses. Rows that change nothing are not counted: they cost almost nothing. Each row is still saved as soon as it is imported. Blocks of 0 rows: no pacing.
FeedImportPacingBlocks = Blocks of %s changed rows, %s seconds apart
FeedImportScheduleUpload = When a file is uploaded
FeedImportNextRun = Next run
FeedImportLastRun = Last run
FeedImportSupplierHelp = The supplier of the feed. Buy prices are recorded as its supplier prices, with the SKU as supplier reference.
FeedImportWarehouseHelp = Warehouse holding this supplier's available stock. Use one warehouse per feed: the feed sets the stock there to the supplier's figures, and to 0 for items that leave the feed. Stock bought for the shop is moved out with a warehouse transfer.
FeedImportWarehouseShared = This warehouse is also used by: %s. Each feed should have its own warehouse, or one feed's figures overwrite the other's.
FeedImportMatchKey = Find existing products by
FeedImportMatchKeyHelp = How an SKU met for the first time is matched with a product Dolibarr already has. Once matched, an item stays linked to its product.
FeedImportMatchSupplierRef = Supplier reference (of this supplier)
FeedImportMatchRef = Product ref (prefix + SKU, or the mapped ref)
FeedImportMatchBarcode = Barcode
FeedImportCreate = Create new products
FeedImportCreateHelp = Items of the feed that match no product are created as products. Items that look like a product Dolibarr already has (same barcode, a typo in the SKU, a ref already used...) go to the review queue instead.
FeedImportRefPrefix = Ref prefix of new products
FeedImportRefPrefixHelp = Added before the SKU to make the ref of new products, e.g. ACME- gives ACME-12345. Recommended: two suppliers may use the same SKUs.
FeedImportCategory = Category of new products
FeedImportVat = Default VAT rate
FeedImportVatHelp = VAT rate of new products and of buy prices when the feed gives none.
FeedImportPriceBase = Selling prices in the feed
FeedImportZero = Set to 0 the stock of items that leave the feed
FeedImportZeroHelp = After a complete import, items no longer in the file get their stock in the feed's warehouse set to 0. Their products are kept.
FeedImportMinRatio = Safety threshold
FeedImportMinRatioHelp = If the file has fewer items than this share of the last import, it is probably truncated: missing items are not set to 0, and the run is marked as a warning.
FeedImportMaxNew = Most new products per run
FeedImportMaxNewHelp = Beyond this, new items go to the review queue: so many at once usually means the supplier changed its SKUs. Not applied on a feed's first import. 0 = no limit.
FeedImportKeep = Files kept
FeedImportNotify = Email on failure
FeedImportNotifyHelp = Addresses (comma separated) emailed when a run fails or needs a look (warning).
FeedImportErrorNoSupplier = Choose the supplier of the feed: existing products are found by this supplier's references.
FeedImportErrorTwice = The Dolibarr field "%s" is mapped twice.
FeedImportErrorSchemaType = The schema must be an XSD file (.xsd) or a two-row CSV file (.csv).
FeedImportErrorXsd = The XSD cannot be used: %s
FeedImportErrorMappingFile = The mapping file cannot be used: %s
FeedImportXsdRead = XSD read: %s fields in the item element %s, %s mapped from its annotations.
FeedImportMappingRead = Mapping file read: %s fields mapped.
